WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.868 --> 00:00:19.609
capture that outlaw Robin Hood one day!"

2
00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:21.991
vowed the Sheriff of Nottingham.

3
00:00:22.891 --> 00:00:27.113
The sheriff was related to the man whom Robin had killed in Sherwood Forest.

4
00:00:28.794 --> 00:00:31.636
But there was another reason the sheriff wanted to catch Robin.

5
00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:37.464
The king was offering a generous reward: two hundred pounds!

6
00:00:39.465 --> 00:00:45.149
But no one wanted to help the sheriff find Robin—not even when he offered a reward too.

7
00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:50.353
People were afraid of the bold outlaw, and many even laughed at the sheriff.

8
00:00:52.835 --> 00:00:54.797
He'd never be able to capture Robin!

9
00:00:56.578 --> 00:00:58.560
This made the sheriff very angry.

10
00:01:00.012 --> 00:01:05.354
"Robin Hood thinks he can get away with breaking the king's laws," said the sheriff to his servants.

11
00:01:05.374 --> 00:01:08.495
"Well, the king will hear about this.

12
00:01:09.275 --> 00:01:11.076
Get everything ready for a trip to London.

13
00:01:11.696 --> 00:01:13.156
We're going to see King Henry!"

14
00:01:14.056 --> 00:01:17.137
For two days the sheriff's servants prepared for the trip.

15
00:01:17.698 --> 00:01:21.419
The sheriff's men polished their armor, eager to impress the king.

16
00:01:22.579 --> 00:01:24.960
At last everyone set off for London.

17
00:01:26.312 --> 00:01:29.374
And what a sight the sheriff and his men made!

18
00:01:30.615 --> 00:01:34.017
People stopped to watch them riding on their fine horses.

19
00:01:35.719 --> 00:01:38.861
The men wore shining armor and fancy clothing.

20
00:01:40.302 --> 00:01:46.586
After two days the sheriff and his men finally reached London, where King Henry lived with Queen Eleanor.

21
00:01:48.127 --> 00:01:50.208
The sheriff and his men were led to the king.

22
00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:53.391
They bowed in front of him.

23
00:01:53.411 --> 00:01:56.229
"Your Majesty," said the sheriff.

24
00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:59.311
"What can I do for you, Sheriff?"

25
00:01:59.912 --> 00:02:00.893
asked King Henry.

26
00:02:00.913 --> 00:02:04.696
"Is there something that you want?"

27
00:02:04.716 --> 00:02:12.162
"As you know, that rascal Robin Hood lives near Nottingham," the sheriff began.

28
00:02:12.182 --> 00:02:16.406
"He kills your deer and robs your loyal men.

29
00:02:17.547 --> 00:02:18.828
I've tried to arrest him.

30
00:02:19.328 --> 00:02:21.490
But I haven't been able to lay a hand on him.

31
00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:23.872
I've come to beg Your Majesty for help."

32
00:02:24.864 --> 00:02:26.365
"You want my help?"

33
00:02:28.606 --> 00:02:31.148
The king's eyes were wide in amazement.

34
00:02:32.288 --> 00:02:35.150
"You come here with all these armed men.

35
00:02:37.551 --> 00:02:39.232
And you can't catch one thief?"

36
00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:46.736
"Well, Your Majesty, Robin is very clever," the sheriff went on.

37
00:02:46.756 --> 00:02:51.339
"He's unlike other outlaws who—" "Get out of my sight!"

38
00:02:51.899 --> 00:02:52.660
roared the king.

39
00:02:54.004 --> 00:02:57.266
"Go back to Nottingham and come up with a plan!

40
00:02:58.667 --> 00:03:03.850
If you can't capture Robin Hood on your own, maybe you shouldn't be sheriff!"

41
00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:06.251
"Yes, Your Majesty.

42
00:03:06.751 --> 00:03:08.112
I'll think of a plan, Your Majesty!"

43
00:03:08.712 --> 00:03:13.175
The sheriff backed away from the king, making one low bow after another.

44
00:03:15.176 --> 00:03:16.977
He groaned quietly to himself.

45
00:03:16.997 --> 00:03:21.640
"I have no idea what to do," he thought.

46
00:03:22.292 --> 00:03:24.795
The group rode slowly back to Nottingham.

47
00:03:25.375 --> 00:03:27.537
The sheriff hung his head during the trip.

48
00:03:28.278 --> 00:03:30.260
At last the sheriff's face lit up.

49
00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:32.101
"Aha!" he cried.

50
00:03:32.121 --> 00:03:33.362
"I've got an idea."

51
00:03:33.382 --> 00:03:34.563
"Ride quickly!"

52
00:03:34.964 --> 00:03:35.865
he ordered his men.

53
00:03:35.885 --> 00:03:37.626
"We have a lot of work to do.

54
00:03:38.327 --> 00:03:41.750
I know how to lure Robin Hood out of the forest and into a trap!"

55
00:03:43.552 --> 00:03:47.936
A few days later the sheriff sent messengers to deliver news across the kingdom.

56
00:03:49.672 --> 00:03:53.214
The sheriff was holding a big archery contest in Nottingham.

57
00:03:54.114 --> 00:03:56.275
First prize was a gold arrow.

58
00:03:57.275 --> 00:04:01.597
The sheriff smiled slyly, delighted with his clever idea.

59
00:04:01.617 --> 00:04:05.859
"Robin Hood won't be able to resist an archery contest.

60
00:04:06.659 --> 00:04:08.820
I'll surely be able to arrest him now!"

61
00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:13.522
And indeed Robin Hood could not resist the contest.

62
00:04:15.062 --> 00:04:18.784
As soon as he heard the news, he gathered his band of men.

63
00:04:19.932 --> 00:04:21.313
"Come, my merry men.

64
00:04:22.114 --> 00:04:23.956
Let's enter this shooting contest.

65
00:04:24.736 --> 00:04:27.439
There's a fine prize of a gold arrow.

66
00:04:28.039 --> 00:04:31.082
And it would annoy the sheriff if one of us won."

67
00:04:31.102 --> 00:04:34.765
"Hooray!" shouted the men.

68
00:04:34.785 --> 00:04:36.947
"Let's do it!"

69
00:04:36.967 --> 00:04:38.888
"Wait, my good master!"

70
00:04:39.309 --> 00:04:41.190
called out David of Doncaster.

71
00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:43.913
"I've just come from the Blue Boar Inn.

72
00:04:44.633 --> 00:04:47.656
I heard something very interesting from some men there.

73
00:04:48.412 --> 00:04:52.635
They say the sheriff wants you to enter the contest so he can capture you.

74
00:04:52.655 --> 00:04:55.076
I believe it's a trap, Robin.

75
00:04:55.636 --> 00:04:58.638
You must stay here in Sherwood Forest where you'll be safe."

76
00:04:58.658 --> 00:05:02.841
"Hmm. Well, maybe we won't go."

77
00:05:03.621 --> 00:05:05.382
Robin was quiet for a moment.

78
00:05:05.402 --> 00:05:10.105
"Oh, but I don't want the sheriff to think I'm afraid of him."

79
00:05:10.765 --> 00:05:11.886
David was worried.

80
00:05:11.906 --> 00:05:14.287
"I told you—it's a trap!"

81
00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:15.068
he said.

82
00:05:15.608 --> 00:05:18.750
"The inn's owner heard it straight from one of the sheriff's men.

83
00:05:19.551 --> 00:05:21.072
I beg you not to go."

84
00:05:21.092 --> 00:05:24.934
"Thank you for the warning, David," said Robin.

85
00:05:24.954 --> 00:05:30.138
"But this news actually makes the contest seem even more interesting."

86
00:05:30.978 --> 00:05:32.679
His eyes twinkled with fun.

87
00:05:32.699 --> 00:05:37.062
"We're sure to have a good time, isn't that so, men?"

88
00:05:37.863 --> 00:05:38.984
His men cheered.

89
00:05:42.617 --> 00:05:45.531
They were all looking forward to the shooting contest!
